 antonio  guterres and according to the un  statement the  russian president vladimir putin has  agreed in principle to  an agreement that would see the united  nations and the international committee  for the red cross uh facilitate the exit  of those civilians that are held uh hold  up in the azov style steel plant and  this evacuation would of course be with  the coordination of the russian defense  ministry as well as ukrainian officials  according to this statement from the  united nations  the russian president and the secretary  general have agreed to conduct a  follow-up discussion with  the un office for the coordination of  humanitarian affairs as well as the  russian defense ministry so  seemingly the impossible task of  achieving any kind of a  resolution to any of the ongoing crises  that are happening in ukraine has been  achieved for now in theory by antonio  guterres now  we understand that this meeting that  lasted two hours between guterres and  putin  was seemingly cordial and they had a lot  to discuss and prior to that meeting  the two men spoke briefly  the russian president saying that he  valued the core principles of  which the united nations was founded on  and russia as one of the founding  members will continue to support this  organization and the important work that  it does he acknowledged that the u.n is  tasked with resolving uh crises that  occur urgently around the world and this  situation in ukraine is certainly one of  them for his part the um secretary  general did not mince any words he held  his ground firmly when addressing  vladimir putin and  reaffirming his belief that this  so-called special military operation by  the russian forces is very much an  invasion uh as far as the united nations  is concerned based on their charter and  it is the um russian forces that have  invaded sovereign territory as a result  of what they believed to be a just cause  but regardless he said that they view it  as an invasion now the two me